# Every text file checks out with LF whatever core.autocrlf says: a CRLF script does not run, and
# check-licences regenerates its JSON from texts in the tree and compares it with the committed copy.
* text=auto eol=lf
# The licence check pins each file's SHA-256 to GNU's edition, so Git must check both out exactly as
# committed. These lines come after the one above because the later line wins. Anchored: other
# LICENSE.md files are not pinned.
/LICENSE.md -text
/COPYING -text
